00:01:39.760 --> 00:01:44.700
With energy in the spotlight, let's look at a mechanical way to generate income from

00:01:44.720 --> 00:01:51.240
quality dividend payers. Passive income ETFs built around high quality dividend payers offer

00:01:51.240 --> 00:01:54.540
a mechanical way to compound without stockpicking risk.

00:01:55.200 --> 00:02:00.580
The approach works by holding a basket of companies with decades-long dividend growth records,

00:02:00.900 --> 00:02:08.040
automatically reinvesting payouts inside a TFSA or RRSP to avoid immediate tax drag.

00:02:08.460 --> 00:02:13.040
In today's environment of elevated rates and selective AI spending,

00:02:13.040 --> 00:02:16.640
these vehicles provide ballast when growth stocks rotate.

00:02:17.300 --> 00:02:21.080
Implementation is straightforward on quest trade or wealth simple.

00:02:21.620 --> 00:02:28.660
Screen for ETFs with 10-plus-year payout histories and expense ratios below 0.25 percent.

00:02:29.100 --> 00:02:30.920
Then dollar cost average monthly.

00:02:31.340 --> 00:02:36.140
The strategy has delivered best results during sideways or modestly rising markets

00:02:36.140 --> 00:02:40.020
when yield plus modest capital appreciation outpaces cash.

00:02:40.900 --> 00:02:46.220
The main risk is sector concentration if the ETF tilts heavily into one industry.

00:02:46.680 --> 00:02:52.500
Always verify the current yield and distribution frequency before allocating more than 15 percent

00:02:52.500 --> 00:02:59.340
of a TFSA sleeve. To get the most from these ETFs, you need to understand the hidden costs that can

00:02:59.340 --> 00:03:06.520
erode compounding. Imagine you bought a passive income ETF last week at the market open after seeing

00:03:06.520 --> 00:03:12.960
the monthly full list. Your 200 share order filled at the ask price of $42.18.

00:03:13.600 --> 00:03:19.500
What actually happened is the ETF's net asset value was calculated at the previous close,

00:03:20.140 --> 00:03:26.260
but the market maker widened the bid-ask spread from 3 cents to 11 cents in the first 15 minutes

00:03:26.260 --> 00:03:33.760
because two large institutional sellers hit the tape. So your effective cost was 0.26 percent higher

00:03:33.760 --> 00:03:40.840
than the NAV. The pro tip most retail investors miss is that limit orders placed at the midpoint

00:03:40.840 --> 00:03:46.780
during the first 30 minutes of trading often get filled inside the spread once volume normalizes,

00:03:47.120 --> 00:03:53.800
whereas market orders pay the full widened spread. The biggest mistake with dividend ETFs is assuming

00:03:53.800 --> 00:04:00.260
the published yield already includes reinvestment friction. Instead, always check the ETF's

00:04:00.260 --> 00:04:05.840
distribution calendar and set a limit order at least one cent inside the current bid before the

00:04:05.840 --> 00:04:11.580
ex-dividend date to capture the full compounding effect without paying unnecessary spread.

